{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780625950,"nonce":"V24UBQ0kT+p3GQaGM15AO8LqcGY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEczXiQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/221","origin":"github"},"title":"Add M3 multibeam transducer frame (base_link → m3) to BizzyBoat URDF","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd the **M3 multibeam transducer frame** (`bizzy/base_link → bizzy/m3`) to the\nBizzyBoat URDF. It's currently missing — the static TF tree has IMU, GNSS, OAK\ncameras, and the DeltaT mount, but no M3, because the M3 is a loaner that was\nnever added to the description.\n\n## Why now\n\nThe M3 → ROS bathymetry path (rolker/marine_tools#1 / PR #14, `kongsberg_em_bridge`)\nis working: it publishes `marine_acoustic_msgs/SonarDetections`, which\n`cube_bathymetry/detections_to_pointcloud` turns into `/soundings` (PointCloud2 in\nthe sonar frame), which `cube_bathymetry_node` georeferences via a **TF lookup to\nthe map frame** and grids into a `GridMap` for CAMP coverage.\n\nWithout an `m3` frame in the TF tree, that lookup fails and nothing georeferences.\nThis frame is the one blocker for live coverage in CAMP. (For the offline surface\nvalidation on 2026-06-04 the transform was hand-injected via\n`static_transform_publisher`.)\n\n## Proposed transform\n\nFrom the hydro install log (#77, `[MEAS]` rough):\n- **x = −0.23 m** (shares the DeltaT cavity), **y = 0.0 m** (centerline),\n  **z = −0.145 m** (transducer face).\n- **rpy = (π, 0, 0)** — roll π for a normally-mounted downward sonar: maps\n  base_link {x-fwd, y-port, z-up} → m3 {x-fwd, y-starboard, z-down}, matching the\n  Kongsberg \"normally mounted looking down\" convention (EM Datagram Formats Note 1)\n  and the `marine_acoustic_msgs/SonarDetections` frame the bridge produces.\n\nThe offsets are rough and the orientation is the nominal convention; a **patch\ntest** confirms/refines both (and resolves handedness — the driver's angle\nconvention is fixed from spec, so the patch test validates this URDF, not a driver\nsign).\n\n## Wiring note\n\nThe bridge stamps `frame_id` (param, default `m3`); set it to `bizzy/m3` in the\nlaunch so it matches this URDF link.\n\nPart of #77.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}